The SSD1306 display never initializes because the I2C pins were assigned to P0.00/P0.01 — the nRF52840's crystal oscillator pins, which are not broken out on the nice_nano_v2 module.

## Changes

- **`9key_makro_master_zmk.overlay`** — Remap I2C from the inaccessible crystal pins to the physically exposed D2/D3 headers:
  ```diff
  - psels = <NRF_PSEL(TWIM_SCL, 0, 1)>,
  -         <NRF_PSEL(TWIM_SDA, 0, 0)>;
  + psels = <NRF_PSEL(TWIM_SCL, 0, 20)>,
  +         <NRF_PSEL(TWIM_SDA, 0, 17)>;
  ```

- **`9key_makro_master_zmk.conf`** — Add `CONFIG_ZMK_DISPLAY_WORK_QUEUE_DEDICATED=y` to give display rendering its own work queue thread, preventing update starvation from other ZMK work items.

